>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `quickcheck`

``` hol4
Refute.quickcheck : term -> outcome
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runs Refute's Quickcheck backends.

`Refute.quickcheck tm` calls `Refute.refute` using `!Refute.the_config`
after forcing backend selection to the Quickcheck backend family,
`SOME ["exhaustive", "random", "narrowing"]`.  Every other field of the
current configuration is preserved, including substrate, size,
iterations, seed, smart-generator options, certification, quiet mode, and
expectations.

The exhaustive and random backends require an executable goal and use the
`Auto`, `NativeSML`, `Cv`, or `Compute` substrate selected by the
configuration.  Narrowing accepts any goal, so it may be the only
applicable backend on a goal the executable ones decline; a returned
counterexample then records `"narrowing"` as its backend.  The
`kodkod` model finder is not selected by this convenience entry point —
use [`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute) for that.

